&lt;p&gt;US President Donald Trump on Thursday angrily confronted a reporter who questioned whether health concerns or exhaustion from his demanding campaign schedule had prompted him to cancel a planned rally in Kansas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The exchange took place after the Republican National Committee (RNC) announced that two of Trump's remaining in-person campaign rallies, scheduled to be held in Kansas and Iowa, would no longer go ahead as planned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dismissing suggestions that his health or the strain of travelling had influenced the decision, Trump insisted that he was feeling well. He made the remarks after returning to Washington from a campaign trip to South Carolina.&lt;/p&gt;
