&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Pentagon's top military planner, Army Lt. Gen. Brett Sylvia, admitted to leaking classified information concerning Ukraine and Iran to two journalists from separate media outlets over a period of one year, according to an internal investigation report shared with Axios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sylvia was dismissed this week by US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth over the alleged misconduct. A US official told Axios that the career military officer acknowledged the leaks on video after failing four polygraph tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The investigation report accused Sylvia of making &quot;unauthorised disclosures to the media&quot;. It also said he struggled to pass multiple polygraph examinations but cooperated with investigators by answering questions about his interactions with journalists and handing over his personal phone for forensic examination.&lt;/p&gt;
